## Update Behaviour

The AxonOps API has no in-place update endpoint for backup schedules. `Update` therefore deletes the existing schedule and creates a new one with the planned configuration. The resource's `id` changes on every update, even when the change is a single attribute such as `local_retention`. Any external system keyed on the old `id` (e.g. a dashboard link or a second Terraform resource referencing `axonops_cassandra_backup.example.id`) MUST be updated after every apply that touches this resource.

